{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Hock&limit=10&title=Birth of the Chaordic Age","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":{"title":"Birth of the chaordic age"},"name":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Hock, Dee",{"@type":"date","#text":"1929-"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"corporate","namePart":"VISA International"}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"cau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"California"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"San Francisco, CA"}}],"publisher":"Berrett-Koehler Publishers","dateIssued":["c1999",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1999"}],"edition":"1st ed.","issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"x, 345 p. ; 25 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"\"The worldwide success of VISA International, Dee Hock asserts, is due to its chaordic structure: it is owned by 22,000 member banks, which both compete with each other for 750 million customers and must cooperate by honoring one another's $1.25 trillion in transactions annually across borders and currencies. Birth of the Chaordic Age is the story of how that structure came into being.\"--Jacket."},"tableOfContents":"In search of a more liveable world -- On the nature and creation of chaordic organizations -- Old monkey mind -- A lamb and the lion of life -- The bloodied sheep -- Retirement on the job -- Ordinary people, extraordinary things -- The house of cards -- Nothing to lose -- The impossible imagined -- The next to the last word -- The corporation or the cane? -- And then there was one -- Quite ordinary people -- The victim of success -- The golden links -- What's in a name? -- The process opens -- The jeweled bearing -- The odyssey -- Then providence moved too -- What can you do -- About the chaordic alliance -- A sample of chaordic alliance participation in the creation of new chaordic organizations.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Dee Hock."},"Includes index."],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Hock, Dee",{"@type":"date","#text":"1929-"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"corporate","namePart":"VISA International"},"topic":"History"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Businessmen","geographic":"United States","genre":"Biography"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Bank credit cards","History"]}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HG1643.H63 A3 1999"},{"@edition":"21","@authority":"ddc","#text":"332.1/78 B"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1576750744 (alk. paper)"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^99044779^"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"42135682"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990082695700203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000011940971X","#text":"Harvard Law School Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HG1643.H63 A3 1999"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000123374118","#text":"Baker Library, Harvard Business School, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HG1643.H63 A3 1999"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HG1643.H63 A3 1999"